1
00:01:54,110 --> 00:01:55,880
Tansy!

2
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,560
-Tansy!  -Tansy!

3
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:18,770
Tansy!

4
00:02:19,260 --> 00:02:20,340
There you are.

5
00:02:24,730 --> 00:02:27,160
I can't see her, Ramsay.

6
00:02:30,890 --> 00:02:32,280
Tansy!

7
00:02:35,670 --> 00:02:38,550
If you make it out of the woods, you win!

8
00:02:38,550 --> 00:02:41,120
Run, Tansy, run!

9
00:02:49,250 --> 00:02:52,500
-Tansy.  -Where is she?

10
00:02:53,310 --> 00:02:55,250
Tansy, Tansy, Tansy!

11
00:03:16,590 --> 00:03:18,770
Good girls. Down, girls.

12
00:03:18,770 --> 00:03:19,810
Down.

13
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:22,920
Well done. You, too.

14
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:23,960
I only wounded her.

15
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:26,300
You brought her down. That's what matters.

16
00:03:26,390 --> 00:03:28,710
A fine shot. Wasn't it, Reek?

17
00:03:28,710 --> 00:03:29,610
A fine shot, master.

18
00:03:29,610 --> 00:03:31,840
-My lady.  -Please, my lord.

19
00:03:32,340 --> 00:03:33,450
It hurts.

20
00:03:33,450 --> 00:03:36,100
Oh, sweet. Don't cry.

21
00:03:36,540 --> 00:03:38,430
It will be over soon.

22
00:03:40,210 --> 00:03:41,660
She thinks she's pretty.

23
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:43,680
Let me put one through her face.

24
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:45,570
We have to reward the hounds, love.

25
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:46,830
They did all the hard work.

26
00:03:46,830 --> 00:03:49,190
Why? I did whatever you asked.

27
00:03:49,190 --> 00:03:51,290
But you made Myranda feel jealous.

28
00:03:51,290 --> 00:03:54,170
-Me jealous of her?  -My lord, please.

29
00:03:54,530 --> 00:03:57,320
You can see that your presence has become a bit of a problem.

30
00:03:59,850 --> 00:04:01,690
Rip her! Rip her!

31
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:02,570
Rip her!

32
00:04:06,230 --> 00:04:07,970
Not so pretty now.

33
00:04:21,440 --> 00:04:23,820
Your new hand, it's nicer than the old one.

34
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:25,750
Wouldn't you agree, Pod?

35
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:27,480
Is it solid gold?

36
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:30,530
Gilded steel. You're not eating.

37
00:04:30,710 --> 00:04:32,560
Why is no one eating?

38
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:35,380
My wife wastes away and my brother starves himself.

39
00:04:35,380 --> 00:04:37,310
-I'm not hungry.  -You lost a hand,

40
00:04:37,530 --> 00:04:38,860
not a stomach.

41
00:04:40,350 --> 00:04:41,240
Try the boar.

42
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:44,360
Cersei can't get enough of it since one killed Robert for her.

43
00:04:46,270 --> 00:04:47,320
A toast.

44
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:50,930
To the proud Lannister children.

45
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:53,890
The dwarf, the cripple, and the mother of madness.

46
00:04:54,510 --> 00:04:55,660
I'll clean it up.

47
00:04:55,660 --> 00:04:57,460
No, I'll do it. Leave us.

48
00:05:00,870 --> 00:05:02,290
It's only wine.

49
00:05:12,430 --> 00:05:13,910
I can't fight anymore.

50
00:05:14,340 --> 00:05:15,740
What about your left?

51
00:05:17,540 --> 00:05:20,080
I can hold a sword, but all my instincts are wrong.

52
00:05:21,450 --> 00:05:22,530
How can I protect the king

53
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:24,310
when I can hardly wipe my own ass?

54
00:05:24,310 --> 00:05:27,370
You're the Lord Commander now. Command.

55
00:05:27,590 --> 00:05:29,030
Let others do the fighting.

56
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:33,320
When was the last time Father used a sword?

57
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:35,520
I'm not Father. I'm the Kingslayer.

58
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:37,800
When people find out I can't slay a pigeon.

59
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:41,080
Train, then. Learn to fight with your other hand.

60
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:44,200
With whom? You? Men talk.

61
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:47,070
Soon as someone discovers I can't fight, he'll tell everyone.

62
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:52,600
You need a proper, discreet swordsman.

63
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:55,930
As it happens, I have just the one.

64
00:06:05,110 --> 00:06:07,290
My brother tells me you can keep your mouth shut.

65
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:09,860
Unusual talent for a sellsword.

66
00:06:10,350 --> 00:06:12,190
He tells me, you shit gold,

67
00:06:12,220 --> 00:06:13,660
just like your father.

68
00:06:15,190 --> 00:06:16,510
Is this place safe?

69
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:21,880
There's this knight, Leygood,

70
00:06:21,930 --> 00:06:24,060
got thunderbolts on his shield.

71
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:26,740
Right here is where I fuck his wife.

72
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:28,750
She's a screamer, that one.

73
00:06:29,470 --> 00:06:31,920
If they don't hear her, they won't hear us.

74
00:06:34,190 --> 00:06:36,020
I've never seen Valyrian steel before.

75
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:38,590
She's a beauty. The problem is,

76
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:40,760
if you fight with an edged blade,

77
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:41,850
I'll have to.

78
00:06:42,730 --> 00:06:44,420
And if I fight with an edged blade,

79
00:06:44,630 --> 00:06:46,280
I'll have no one left to pay me.

80
00:06:48,060 --> 00:06:51,000
I haven't used a sparring sword since I was nine.

81
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:00,910
Bold warrior you are, attacking a man when his guard's down.

82
00:07:00,910 --> 00:07:02,390
Best time to attack a man.

83
00:07:05,250 --> 00:07:06,370
Mind yourself.

84
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:10,580
If I still had my right hand.

85
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:11,700
Plan on growing it back?

86
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:27,950
Come on, then.

87
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:41,680
Open the gates!

88
00:07:43,390 --> 00:07:44,830
Riders coming in!

89
00:08:01,530 --> 00:08:03,700
Let's get these horses seen to!

90
00:08:06,650 --> 00:08:08,470
Father. Welcome home.

91
00:08:08,670 --> 00:08:11,130
Walda, this is Ramsay Snow, my bastard.

92
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:13,620
A pleasure, Mother.

93
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:16,720
Hello.

94
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:19,210
See that the horses are fed, watered, and rubbed down.

95
00:08:19,210 --> 00:08:21,040
And take Lady Walda to her chambers.

96
00:08:22,690 --> 00:08:23,740
This way, my lady.

97
00:08:25,130 --> 00:08:26,530
Where is your prize?

98
00:08:27,060 --> 00:08:28,290
With the hounds.

99
00:08:29,630 --> 00:08:30,780
I'll have a look at him.

100
00:08:37,630 --> 00:08:39,790
I hear you took a hand from the Kingslayer.

101
00:08:39,790 --> 00:08:42,430
Word travels. How he screamed.

102
00:08:42,740 --> 00:08:44,140
You would have loved it.

103
00:08:54,590 --> 00:08:55,410
Father.

104
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:06,400
What did you do to him?

105
00:09:06,670 --> 00:09:11,290
I trained him. He was a slow learner, but he learned.

106
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:13,330
You flayed him.

107
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:15,380
Peeled a few bits.

108
00:09:16,040 --> 00:09:17,560
Removed a few others.

109
00:09:20,770 --> 00:09:22,860
This was Balon Greyjoy's son and heir.

110
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:25,530
We've been flaying our enemies for 1,000 years.

111
00:09:25,990 --> 00:09:27,510
The flayed man is on our banners.

112
00:09:27,510 --> 00:09:29,150
My banners, not yours.

113
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:31,330
You're not a Bolton. You're a Snow.

114
00:09:35,230 --> 00:09:37,400
Tywin Lannister has given me the North.

115
00:09:37,510 --> 00:09:39,810
But he won't lift a finger to help me take it.

116
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,050
As long as the ironborn hold Moat Cailin,

117
00:09:42,050 --> 00:09:44,190
our armies are trapped south of the Neck.

118
00:09:44,650 --> 00:09:47,830
Theon was a valuable hostage, not your plaything.

119
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:51,110
I wanted to trade him for Moat Cailin.

120
00:09:51,110 --> 00:09:52,530
I already asked.

121
00:09:52,990 --> 00:09:56,640
Lord Greyjoy refused. Savages have no.

122
00:09:56,640 --> 00:09:59,240
You sent terms to Balon Greyjoy without my consent?

123
00:09:59,240 --> 00:10:01,560
You made me acting Lord of the Dreadfort.

124
00:10:02,010 --> 00:10:03,240
I acted.

125
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:11,350
I had to smuggle myself into my own lands

126
00:10:11,350 --> 00:10:13,020
thanks to the Greyjoys.

127
00:10:13,690 --> 00:10:15,230
I needed Theon.

128
00:10:15,790 --> 00:10:17,490
I needed him whole.

129
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:20,300
Theon was our enemy.

130
00:10:21,230 --> 00:10:22,440
But Reek,

131
00:10:23,580 --> 00:10:25,610
Reek will never betray us.

132
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:29,170
I placed far too much trust in you.

133
00:10:38,530 --> 00:10:42,400
Reek, how could you let me stand before my father unshaven?

134
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:45,550
-It's disrespectful.  -I'm sorry, my lord.

135
00:10:47,770 --> 00:10:48,820
Give him the razor.

136
00:10:58,090 --> 00:11:01,430
I'm not a Bolton, father, what does it matter?

137
00:11:09,370 --> 00:11:10,480
Go on, Reek.

138
00:11:10,850 --> 00:11:13,150
A nice close shave.

139
00:11:33,630 --> 00:11:36,930
Reek, tell father,

140
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:40,310
where are Bran and Rickon Stark?

141
00:11:41,020 --> 00:11:42,470
I don't know, my lord.

142
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:43,940
You murdered them

143
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:47,580
and displayed their corpses at Winterfell.

144
00:11:48,470 --> 00:11:49,370
Reek,

145
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:53,650
did you murder the Stark boys?

146
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:55,260
No, my lord.

147
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,380
Just two farm boys.

148
00:11:57,550 --> 00:12:00,100
And crisped them, so no one would know.

149
00:12:00,810 --> 00:12:01,950
Yes, my lord.

150
00:12:04,780 --> 00:12:07,180
The Starks have always ruled the North.

151
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:09,930
If Bran and Rickon are alive,

152
00:12:09,940 --> 00:12:12,120
the country will rally to their side

153
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:14,620
now that Robb Stark is gone.

154
00:12:17,060 --> 00:12:19,630
Oh, that's right, Reek.

155
00:12:21,570 --> 00:12:23,200
Robb Stark is dead.

156
00:12:24,470 --> 00:12:25,350
Sorry.

157
00:12:26,490 --> 00:12:28,600
I know he was like a brother to you.

158
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:31,420
But my father put a knife through his heart.

159
00:12:34,470 --> 00:12:36,200
How do you feel about that?

160
00:12:50,410 --> 00:12:52,350
-You ready for a hunt?  -Always.

161
00:12:52,350 --> 00:12:55,750
Find those boys and I'll give you 1,000 acres and a holdfast.

162
00:12:56,060 --> 00:12:57,740
Your pet rat have any thoughts

163
00:12:57,740 --> 00:12:59,950
on which way they went after Winterfell?

164
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:04,610
Jon Snow is at Castle Black.

165
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:07,490
Who the fuck is Jon Snow?

166
00:13:07,540 --> 00:13:09,110
Their bastard brother.

167
00:13:09,700 --> 00:13:11,220
He could be sheltering them.

168
00:13:11,490 --> 00:13:12,880
He may know where they are.

169
00:13:14,610 --> 00:13:18,100
Even if he doesn't, he's half Stark himself.

170
00:13:18,510 --> 00:13:19,770
Could be a threat.

171
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:21,960
You want to prove yourself a Bolton?

172
00:13:22,810 --> 00:13:25,550
Gather whatever men you can and ride for Moat Cailin.

173
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:28,010
Bring this creature of yours.

174
00:13:29,040 --> 00:13:30,780
Maybe he'll be of some use.

175
00:13:33,940 --> 00:13:35,540
Take the Moat for the family,

176
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:37,190
for our family,

177
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:39,540
and I'll reconsider your position.

178
00:13:43,400 --> 00:13:46,200
Lord Varys. Breakfasting with the king?

179
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:49,610
I'm afraid foreigners aren't welcome at such exclusive affairs.

180
00:13:49,610 --> 00:13:51,220
Oh, to be foreign.

181
00:13:53,030 --> 00:13:54,370
Shae has been noticed.

182
00:13:54,370 --> 00:13:56,040
Sansa's maid saw you with her.

183
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:57,660
She already told your sister.

184
00:13:57,670 --> 00:14:00,200
It's only a matter of time before your father hears.

185
00:14:00,690 --> 00:14:03,330
So I'm guilty of being seen with my own wife's handmaiden.

186
00:14:03,330 --> 00:14:05,350
My father will ask you if there's anything more

187
00:14:05,350 --> 00:14:06,800
and you'll tell him some clever lie.

188
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:08,550
No, I will not.

189
00:14:08,780 --> 00:14:11,560
How long do you imagine your father and sister would let me live

190
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:13,680
if they suspected me of lying?

191
00:14:14,050 --> 00:14:16,570
I have no pet sellsword to protect me.

192
00:14:16,570 --> 00:14:19,160
No legendary brother to avenge me.

193
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:21,270
Only little birds who whisper in my ear.

194
00:14:21,270 --> 00:14:23,180
Forgive me if I don't weep for you.

195
00:14:23,350 --> 00:14:26,130
No one weeps for spiders or whores.

196
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:29,070
I have friends across the sea who could help her.

197
00:14:29,070 --> 00:14:30,400
She won't leave.

198
00:14:30,460 --> 00:14:32,210
I've told her this is a dangerous place

199
00:14:32,210 --> 00:14:34,060
so many times, she no longer believes it.

200
00:14:34,060 --> 00:14:34,970
Your father has promised

201
00:14:34,970 --> 00:14:37,390
to hang the next whore he finds you with.

202
00:14:37,390 --> 00:14:40,420
Have you ever known your father to make an idle threat?

203
00:14:43,390 --> 00:14:46,420
From House Tyrell and the people of the Reach,

204
00:14:46,560 --> 00:14:49,880
Your Grace, it is my honor to present you with this wedding cup.

205
00:14:50,900 --> 00:14:52,750
May you and my daughter Margaery

206
00:14:52,750 --> 00:14:55,000
drink deep and live long.

207
00:14:55,490 --> 00:14:57,030
A handsome goblet, my lord.

208
00:14:57,510 --> 00:14:59,620
Or shall I call you Father?

209
00:14:59,830 --> 00:15:01,600
I shall be honored, Your Grace.

210
00:15:09,670 --> 00:15:11,910
She's the whore I told you about.

211
00:15:11,910 --> 00:15:13,100
The dark-haired one.

212
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:18,140
Have her brought to the Tower of the Hand before the wedding.

213
00:15:28,990 --> 00:15:29,920
A book?

214
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:32,750
"The Lives of Four Kings." Grand Maester Kaeth's history

215
00:15:32,750 --> 00:15:35,570
of the reigns of Daeron the Young Dragon,

216
00:15:35,710 --> 00:15:37,330
Baelor the Blessed,

217
00:15:37,330 --> 00:15:39,500
Aegon the Unworthy, and Daeron the Good.

218
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:41,370
A book every king should read.

219
00:15:50,870 --> 00:15:52,270
Now that the war is won,

220
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:55,540
we should all find time for wisdom.

221
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:58,290
Thank you, Uncle.

222
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:13,420
One of only two Valyrian steel swords in the capital,

223
00:16:13,420 --> 00:16:17,100
Your Grace, freshly forged in your honor.

224
00:16:30,270 --> 00:16:34,260
Careful, Your Grace. Nothing cuts like Valyrian steel.

225
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:35,400
So they say.

226
00:16:47,780 --> 00:16:49,790
Such a great sword should have a name.

227
00:16:49,790 --> 00:16:52,930
-What shall I call her?  -Stormbringer.

228
00:16:52,930 --> 00:16:54,880
-Terminus.  -Widow's Wail.

229
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:57,320
-Wolfsbane.  -Widow's Wail. I like that.

230
00:16:59,830 --> 00:17:01,790
Every time I use it, it'll be like cutting off

231
00:17:01,790 --> 00:17:03,860
Ned Stark's head all over again.

232
00:17:31,810 --> 00:17:32,750
Don't.

233
00:17:36,010 --> 00:17:37,360
You want me on the desk?

234
00:17:40,490 --> 00:17:42,880
-What's wrong, my lion?  -Don't call me that.

235
00:17:43,450 --> 00:17:45,100
What should I call you?

236
00:17:46,210 --> 00:17:48,450
I'm afraid our friendship can't continue.

237
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:51,230
Our friendship?

238
00:17:51,230 --> 00:17:53,670
There's a ship waiting in the harbor bound for Pentos.

239
00:17:54,990 --> 00:17:55,930
What?

240
00:17:55,930 --> 00:17:57,670
You'll have your own cabin, of course,

241
00:17:57,670 --> 00:18:01,450
and across the Narrow Sea a house, servants.

242
00:18:03,370 --> 00:18:04,720
What is this?

243
00:18:04,760 --> 00:18:06,230
I'm a married man.

244
00:18:07,290 --> 00:18:10,060
My wife has suffered a great deal, as you well know.

245
00:18:10,060 --> 00:18:12,590
I don't want her to suffer anymore on my account.

246
00:18:12,590 --> 00:18:14,750
I need to uphold my vows.

247
00:18:16,050 --> 00:18:17,680
She doesn't want you.

248
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:20,400
-I need to do right by her.  -You don't want her.

249
00:18:20,410 --> 00:18:22,100
By our children.

250
00:18:24,470 --> 00:18:26,250
-What are you afraid of?  -I'm not afraid.

251
00:18:26,250 --> 00:18:30,030
You are. You are afraid of your father and your sister.

252
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:30,870
You're going to run from

253
00:18:30,870 --> 00:18:32,610
-them all your life?  -I need you to leave.

254
00:18:32,610 --> 00:18:35,500
I'm not afraid of them. I'm not going to run from them.

255
00:18:35,500 --> 00:18:37,420
-Shae.  -We will fight them together.

256
00:18:37,430 --> 00:18:40,030
It's like you said, I am yours and you are mine.

257
00:18:40,030 --> 00:18:41,010
You're a whore!

258
00:18:44,330 --> 00:18:48,140
Sansa is fit to bear my children and you are not.

259
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:50,280
I can't be in love with a whore.

260
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:52,720
I can't have children with a whore.

261
00:18:53,450 --> 00:18:55,390
How many men have you been with?

262
00:18:55,390 --> 00:18:57,290
500? 5,000?

263
00:19:03,610 --> 00:19:05,650
How many whores have you been with?

264
00:19:05,650 --> 00:19:07,780
I have enjoyed my time with all of them

265
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:10,170
and I have enjoyed my time with you most of all.

266
00:19:10,170 --> 00:19:11,850
But now that time is over.

267
00:19:28,410 --> 00:19:31,060
You'll have a comfortable life in Pentos.

268
00:19:33,670 --> 00:19:35,600
Bronn will escort you to your ship.

269
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:03,520
Hear us now.

270
00:20:04,050 --> 00:20:07,160
Accept these tokens of our faith, my lord,

271
00:20:07,310 --> 00:20:09,280
and lead us from the darkness.

272
00:20:10,310 --> 00:20:13,510
Sire, I served you well.

273
00:20:13,510 --> 00:20:15,530
Lord of Light, show us the way.

274
00:20:16,540 --> 00:20:20,100
Selyse, you're my sister!

275
00:20:20,370 --> 00:20:22,340
Yours are the stars that guide us.

276
00:20:22,340 --> 00:20:23,990
Tell him! Tell him!

277
00:20:23,990 --> 00:20:25,850
Lord of Light, protect us,

278
00:20:26,190 --> 00:20:29,290
for the night is dark and full of terrors.

279
00:20:40,910 --> 00:20:43,650
Did you see? Their souls.

280
00:20:44,120 --> 00:20:45,810
It was their souls.

281
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:48,920
Our lord took them. Did you see?

282
00:20:55,530 --> 00:20:58,520
Lord Florent was your brother by law.

283
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:00,900
He was an infidel.

284
00:21:01,580 --> 00:21:03,420
He worshipped the gods of his fathers

285
00:21:03,420 --> 00:21:05,510
and their fathers before him.

286
00:21:05,730 --> 00:21:08,140
They were the gods of your fathers, too.

287
00:21:08,540 --> 00:21:10,390
I ordered him to tear down his idols.

288
00:21:10,390 --> 00:21:11,720
He disobeyed.

289
00:21:11,960 --> 00:21:14,050
How many ships did he bring to your cause?

290
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:15,600
How many men?

291
00:21:15,600 --> 00:21:17,060
A good deal more than you.

292
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:21,020
Did you see, Ser Davos?

293
00:21:21,340 --> 00:21:22,580
They're with our lord now.

294
00:21:22,580 --> 00:21:25,230
Their sins all burned away. Did you see?

295
00:21:25,410 --> 00:21:27,680
I'm sure they're more than grateful, my queen.

296
00:21:42,470 --> 00:21:43,580
Meat's off.

297
00:21:45,520 --> 00:21:47,400
Our larders are almost empty.

298
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:49,780
Serve fish, then. We're on an island.

299
00:21:49,780 --> 00:21:51,170
You hate fish.

300
00:21:51,260 --> 00:21:54,160
I hate a good many things, but I suffer them all the same.

301
00:21:56,100 --> 00:21:59,510
When Storm's End was under siege and I was starving,

302
00:21:59,880 --> 00:22:03,420
Stannis boiled soup for me from books.

303
00:22:04,560 --> 00:22:06,650
The binding glue is made from horses.

304
00:22:09,870 --> 00:22:14,450
One morning, he shot two seagulls on the beach.

305
00:22:14,450 --> 00:22:17,680
I've never tasted anything as good as grilled seagull.

306
00:22:19,620 --> 00:22:21,720
-Do you remember?  -Of course I remember.

307
00:22:25,060 --> 00:22:27,100
Have you ever known true hunger, my lady?

308
00:22:27,950 --> 00:22:30,020
It's all I knew when I was a child.

309
00:22:30,020 --> 00:22:31,730
Until you found the Lord of Light?

310
00:22:31,910 --> 00:22:33,810
Until he found me.

311
00:22:41,300 --> 00:22:43,310
I fear for our daughter's soul.

312
00:22:44,740 --> 00:22:46,950
Every mother should fear for her child's soul.

313
00:22:46,950 --> 00:22:49,400
-She's a stubborn little beast.  -She's a child.

314
00:22:49,630 --> 00:22:51,100
You barely know her.

315
00:22:51,360 --> 00:22:53,930
You think she's sweet, because she smiles when you visit.

316
00:22:53,990 --> 00:22:56,910
She's sullen and stubborn and sinful.

317
00:22:57,120 --> 00:22:59,830
Why else would the Lord of Light have seen fit to mark her face?

318
00:22:59,830 --> 00:23:01,070
She needs the rod.

319
00:23:01,080 --> 00:23:04,400
She's my daughter. You will not strike her.

320
00:23:06,180 --> 00:23:07,590
As you command.

321
00:23:09,440 --> 00:23:11,620
Perhaps the Lady Melisandre could speak with her.

322
00:23:20,140 --> 00:23:21,130
Come in.

323
00:23:23,990 --> 00:23:25,830
Were you sleeping, Princess?

324
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:32,990
Did you watch the ceremony on the beach?

325
00:23:33,390 --> 00:23:34,780
I heard it.

326
00:23:35,770 --> 00:23:37,190
And it frightened you?

327
00:23:37,530 --> 00:23:39,370
Ser Axel was my uncle.

328
00:23:39,610 --> 00:23:41,310
He was always kind to me.

329
00:23:41,310 --> 00:23:43,220
They're in a better place now, Princess.

330
00:23:43,220 --> 00:23:46,000
The fire cleansed them of the sins of the world.

331
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:47,450
But they screamed.

332
00:23:47,610 --> 00:23:49,540
Women scream when they give birth.

333
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:52,410
Afterward they are filled with joy.

334
00:23:52,410 --> 00:23:53,990
Afterward they aren't ash and bone.

335
00:23:53,990 --> 00:23:56,280
You have so many questions, don't you?

336
00:23:56,760 --> 00:23:58,560
So did I when I was a child.

337
00:23:58,890 --> 00:24:00,320
I was much like you.

338
00:24:01,510 --> 00:24:03,260
Only I wasn't a princess.

339
00:24:03,440 --> 00:24:05,010
And you didn't have this.

340
00:24:05,010 --> 00:24:06,080
No.

341
00:24:07,230 --> 00:24:09,860
But I suffered in other ways, sweet girl, believe me.

342
00:24:10,920 --> 00:24:12,570
What do you know of the gods?

343
00:24:13,080 --> 00:24:15,010
I read "The Seven-Pointed Star."

344
00:24:15,420 --> 00:24:17,190
Lies and fables.

345
00:24:18,090 --> 00:24:20,000
Septons speak of seven gods.

346
00:24:20,010 --> 00:24:21,670
There are but two,

347
00:24:21,680 --> 00:24:24,370
a god of light and love and joy

348
00:24:24,630 --> 00:24:28,030
and a god of darkness, evil, and fear.

349
00:24:28,350 --> 00:24:30,080
Eternally at war.

350
00:24:30,270 --> 00:24:34,260
There are no seven heavens and no seven hells?

351
00:24:34,790 --> 00:24:37,820
There's only one hell, Princess.

352
00:24:38,460 --> 00:24:40,300
The one we live in now.

353
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:16,730
Hodor.

354
00:25:22,320 --> 00:25:23,520
Why did you wake me?

355
00:25:23,530 --> 00:25:25,030
You've been gone for hours.

356
00:25:26,430 --> 00:25:27,630
I was hungry.

357
00:25:28,790 --> 00:25:30,210
We're all hungry.

358
00:25:30,770 --> 00:25:32,220
I was just eating.

359
00:25:32,220 --> 00:25:33,690
Summer was eating.

360
00:25:34,690 --> 00:25:37,780
Your body can't live on the food your wolf consumes.

361
00:25:38,080 --> 00:25:40,970
Spending too much time in Summer's skin is dangerous.

362
00:25:42,250 --> 00:25:44,370
You're not a direwolf, Bran.

363
00:25:47,240 --> 00:25:48,940
Must be glorious, though.

364
00:25:49,500 --> 00:25:53,160
To run, to leap, to hunt.

365
00:25:54,320 --> 00:25:55,840
To be whole.

366
00:25:57,070 --> 00:25:58,390
I know that's tempting,

367
00:25:59,350 --> 00:26:00,990
but if you're trapped in Summer for too long,

368
00:26:00,990 --> 00:26:03,000
you'll forget what it was to be human.

369
00:26:07,370 --> 00:26:08,940
You'd forget us, Bran.

370
00:26:09,570 --> 00:26:11,040
You'd forget your mother and father.

371
00:26:11,050 --> 00:26:13,200
You'd forget your brothers and sisters.

372
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:14,920
You'd forget Winterfell.

373
00:26:15,700 --> 00:26:17,420
You'd forget you.

374
00:26:17,420 --> 00:26:21,250
And if we lose you, we lose everything.

375
00:26:52,690 --> 00:26:55,520
Hodor, take me to the tree.

376
00:27:43,740 --> 00:27:45,240
Look for me,

377
00:27:51,470 --> 00:27:53,280
beneath the tree.

378
00:27:57,330 --> 00:27:58,460
He saw us.

379
00:28:03,340 --> 00:28:04,500
North.

380
00:28:14,330 --> 00:28:15,720
I know where we have to go.

381
00:29:03,900 --> 00:29:06,690
Let it be known that Margaery of House Tyrell

382
00:29:07,150 --> 00:29:10,210
and Joffrey of the Houses Lannister and Baratheon

383
00:29:10,760 --> 00:29:14,670
are one heart, one flesh, one soul.

384
00:29:15,820 --> 00:29:19,380
Cursed be he who would seek to tear them asunder.

385
00:29:22,770 --> 00:29:27,000
With this kiss, I pledge my love.

386
00:29:48,570 --> 00:29:50,090
We have a new queen.

387
00:29:52,790 --> 00:29:54,400
Better her than you.

388
00:30:06,750 --> 00:30:09,180
-Bit much, wouldn't you say?  -It feels proportionate.

389
00:30:09,180 --> 00:30:12,510
-Proportionate to what?  -The expected extravagance.

390
00:30:12,570 --> 00:30:14,960
People who spend their money on this sort of nonsense

391
00:30:14,960 --> 00:30:16,630
tend not to have it for long.

392
00:30:16,630 --> 00:30:19,950
You ought to try enjoying something before you die.

393
00:30:20,020 --> 00:30:21,560
You might find it suits you.

394
00:30:21,560 --> 00:30:24,760
Not now, Mace. Lord Tywin and I are speaking.

395
00:30:25,080 --> 00:30:27,450
Anyway, I don't know what you're complaining about.

396
00:30:27,450 --> 00:30:29,070
I'm paying my share.

397
00:30:29,070 --> 00:30:31,520
Shall we stick golden roses in half the meat pies

398
00:30:31,520 --> 00:30:33,250
to commemorate your generosity?

399
00:30:33,250 --> 00:30:36,690
No, your heartfelt thank-you is its own reward.

400
00:30:36,940 --> 00:30:39,680
I would imagine, I'd be hearing it again before long.

401
00:30:39,720 --> 00:30:41,990
Wars are rather expensive.

402
00:30:42,080 --> 00:30:44,770
"The Iron Bank will have its due."

403
00:30:45,170 --> 00:30:47,550
How they love to remind everyone.

404
00:30:47,620 --> 00:30:50,350
Almost as much as you Lannisters with your debts.

405
00:30:50,350 --> 00:30:52,530
I'm not worried about the Iron Bank.

406
00:30:52,530 --> 00:30:54,890
We both know you're smarter than that.

407
00:30:55,490 --> 00:30:59,150
Come, Tywin, let us celebrate young love.

408
00:31:11,320 --> 00:31:12,940
All taken care of.

409
00:31:13,020 --> 00:31:16,160
-You saw her board the ship?  -Aye, she's on it.

410
00:31:16,360 --> 00:31:18,080
You saw the ship sail away?

411
00:31:18,590 --> 00:31:21,370
No one knows she's there but you, me, and Varys.

412
00:31:21,580 --> 00:31:22,800
How do you know?

413
00:31:23,230 --> 00:31:25,900
Because if someone follows me without an invitation,

414
00:31:25,910 --> 00:31:27,880
I'm the last person they ever follow.

415
00:31:27,880 --> 00:31:29,530
There's someone following you?

416
00:31:31,410 --> 00:31:32,450
She's gone.

417
00:31:33,350 --> 00:31:35,570
I know you don't want to believe it, but she is.

418
00:31:35,570 --> 00:31:38,970
Now, go drink till it feels like you did the right thing.

419
00:31:45,220 --> 00:31:46,100
Hello.

420
00:31:47,160 --> 00:31:48,850
-Hello.  -Not you.

421
00:32:05,940 --> 00:32:07,990
You look exquisite, child.

422
00:32:08,700 --> 00:32:10,700
The wind has been at you, though.

423
00:32:11,870 --> 00:32:14,300
I haven't had the opportunity to tell you

424
00:32:14,570 --> 00:32:17,230
how sorry I was to hear about your brother.

425
00:32:17,920 --> 00:32:21,030
War is war, but killing a man at a wedding,

426
00:32:21,360 --> 00:32:22,480
horrid.

427
00:32:22,700 --> 00:32:24,950
What sort of monster would do such a thing?

428
00:32:25,240 --> 00:32:28,150
As if men need more reasons to fear marriage.

429
00:32:28,160 --> 00:32:29,700
My lady. My lady.

430
00:32:29,700 --> 00:32:33,140
Lord Tyrion, you see? Not as bad as all that.

431
00:32:33,150 --> 00:32:34,710
Perhaps if your pauper husband

432
00:32:34,710 --> 00:32:37,570
were to sell his mule and his last pair of shoes,

433
00:32:37,570 --> 00:32:40,720
he might be able to afford to bring you to Highgarden for a visit.

434
00:32:40,720 --> 00:32:43,810
Now that peace has come and all is right with the world,

435
00:32:43,810 --> 00:32:46,170
it would do you good to see some of it.

436
00:32:46,270 --> 00:32:48,820
You must excuse me. It's time I ate

437
00:32:48,820 --> 00:32:51,380
some of this food I paid for.

438
00:32:54,140 --> 00:33:00,250
In a coat of gold or a coat of red

439
00:33:00,250 --> 00:33:06,490
a lion still has claws,

440
00:33:06,520 --> 00:33:09,050
And mine, my lord.

441
00:33:09,050 --> 00:33:11,280
Very good. Very good. Off you go.

442
00:33:27,450 --> 00:33:30,490
My love, why don't we make the announcement?

443
00:33:32,870 --> 00:33:33,930
Everyone.

444
00:33:35,420 --> 00:33:38,460
The queen would like to say a few words.

445
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:47,930
We are so fortunate

446
00:33:47,930 --> 00:33:50,300
to enjoy this marvelous food and drink.

447
00:33:50,300 --> 00:33:52,410
Not all among us are so lucky.

448
00:33:52,690 --> 00:33:56,790
To thank the gods for bringing the recent war to a just end,

449
00:33:57,060 --> 00:33:59,430
King Joffrey has decreed

450
00:33:59,430 --> 00:34:01,610
that the leftovers from our feast

451
00:34:01,620 --> 00:34:03,810
be given to the poorest in his city.

452
00:34:15,470 --> 00:34:17,240
You're an example to us all.

453
00:34:34,250 --> 00:34:35,950
Ser Jaime, I'm very sorry.

454
00:34:35,960 --> 00:34:37,410
Ser Loras, it's quite all right.

455
00:34:40,480 --> 00:34:42,070
Your sister looks very beautiful.

456
00:34:42,700 --> 00:34:43,770
As does yours.

457
00:34:44,110 --> 00:34:46,690
So, looking forward to your wedding?

458
00:34:47,450 --> 00:34:49,340
Yes, very much.

459
00:34:49,350 --> 00:34:51,820
Our fathers are both rather keen on the prospect.

460
00:34:52,220 --> 00:34:53,220
They certainly are.

461
00:34:53,230 --> 00:34:54,600
Perhaps they should get married.

462
00:34:57,040 --> 00:35:00,710
If you were to marry Cersei, she'd murder you in your sleep.

463
00:35:01,130 --> 00:35:04,740
If you somehow managed to put a child in her first,

464
00:35:04,770 --> 00:35:06,280
she'd murder him, too,

465
00:35:06,550 --> 00:35:08,200
long before he drew his first breath.

466
00:35:08,880 --> 00:35:11,450
Luckily for you, none of this will happen,

467
00:35:11,880 --> 00:35:13,640
because you'll never marry her.

468
00:35:17,580 --> 00:35:18,780
And neither will you.

469
00:35:33,200 --> 00:35:35,650
Your Grace. My king. My queen.

470
00:35:35,670 --> 00:35:36,690
Lady Brienne.

471
00:35:37,750 --> 00:35:39,080
So good of you to come.

472
00:35:39,210 --> 00:35:40,450
I'm no lady, Your Grace.

473
00:35:40,450 --> 00:35:41,770
Did you just bow?

474
00:35:43,180 --> 00:35:44,510
Apologies, Your Grace.

475
00:35:44,970 --> 00:35:46,740
I never did master the curtsy.

476
00:35:46,740 --> 00:35:49,150
You're the one who put a sword through Renly Baratheon.

477
00:35:49,150 --> 00:35:51,760
That's not true, my love. Brienne had nothing to do with it.

478
00:35:52,490 --> 00:35:53,300
A shame.

479
00:35:53,780 --> 00:35:56,490
I'd knight the man that put an end to that deviant's life.

480
00:35:57,570 --> 00:36:00,840
I just wanted to congratulate you both and wish you good fortune.

481
00:36:00,900 --> 00:36:02,680
The country has been at war too long.

482
00:36:03,840 --> 00:36:06,360
I hope your reign is long and peaceful.

483
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:07,790
-Yes, yes.  -Thank you.

484
00:36:08,170 --> 00:36:09,650
I hope we see more of you.

485
00:36:17,570 --> 00:36:18,520
Lady Brienne.

486
00:36:20,100 --> 00:36:21,900
You're Lord Selwyn Tarth's daughter.

487
00:36:22,470 --> 00:36:25,240
That makes you a lady whether you want to be or not.

488
00:36:25,610 --> 00:36:26,840
As you say, your Grace.

489
00:36:27,080 --> 00:36:28,560
I owe you my gratitude.

490
00:36:28,700 --> 00:36:31,070
You returned my brother safely to King's Landing.

491
00:36:33,970 --> 00:36:35,830
In truth, he rescued me, Your Grace.

492
00:36:36,580 --> 00:36:37,710
More than once.

493
00:36:38,700 --> 00:36:39,570
Did he?

494
00:36:41,100 --> 00:36:42,670
Haven't heard that story before.

495
00:36:44,590 --> 00:36:46,740
Not such a fascinating story, I'm afraid.

496
00:36:46,740 --> 00:36:49,120
I'm sure you have many fascinating stories.

497
00:36:49,680 --> 00:36:50,820
Sworn to Renly Baratheon.

498
00:36:50,820 --> 00:36:52,160
Sworn to Catelyn Stark.

499
00:36:52,170 --> 00:36:53,410
And now my brother.

500
00:36:53,720 --> 00:36:56,890
Must be exciting to flit from one camp to the next

501
00:36:57,200 --> 00:36:59,590
serving whichever lord or lady you fancy.

502
00:36:59,780 --> 00:37:02,080
I don't serve your brother, your Grace.

503
00:37:03,140 --> 00:37:04,160
But you love him.

504
00:37:12,630 --> 00:37:13,470
Your Grace.

505
00:37:25,020 --> 00:37:28,710
No, no, come to my chambers and I will examine you personally.

506
00:37:28,710 --> 00:37:31,180
-She'll do no such thing.  -Oh, Your Grace.

507
00:37:31,180 --> 00:37:33,770
Yes, well, this young lady sought my advice.

508
00:37:33,770 --> 00:37:35,480
You should see Qyburn. He's quite good.

509
00:37:35,480 --> 00:37:38,220
-Your Grace.  -Qyburn? Deplorable man.

510
00:37:38,470 --> 00:37:41,410
Brought shame on the Citadel with his repugnant experiments.

511
00:37:41,410 --> 00:37:43,820
More repugnant than your gnarled fingers on that girl's thighs?

512
00:37:43,820 --> 00:37:46,300
Your Grace, I am a man of learning.

513
00:37:46,300 --> 00:37:48,550
My little brother had you sent to the Black Cells

514
00:37:48,560 --> 00:37:49,510
when you annoyed him.

515
00:37:49,510 --> 00:37:51,590
What do you think I could do to you if you annoyed me?

516
00:37:51,590 --> 00:37:53,730
I never meant to annoy anyone.

517
00:37:53,730 --> 00:37:56,050
But you are. You annoy me right now.

518
00:37:56,380 --> 00:37:58,570
Every breath you draw in my presence annoys me.

519
00:37:58,570 --> 00:37:59,750
So here's what I want you to do.

520
00:37:59,760 --> 00:38:01,410
I want you to leave my presence.

521
00:38:01,460 --> 00:38:03,070
Leave this wedding right now.

522
00:38:03,070 --> 00:38:04,650
Go to the kitchens and instruct them

523
00:38:04,650 --> 00:38:07,020
that all the leftovers from the feast

524
00:38:07,020 --> 00:38:08,290
will be brought to the kennels.

525
00:38:08,290 --> 00:38:10,770
Your Grace, Queen Margaery.

526
00:38:10,770 --> 00:38:12,800
The queen is telling you

527
00:38:13,100 --> 00:38:14,990
the leftovers will feed the dogs

528
00:38:15,840 --> 00:38:16,990
or you will.

529
00:38:36,880 --> 00:38:39,520
A gold dragon to whoever knocks my fool's hat off.

530
00:38:51,410 --> 00:38:52,870
You're in rather a good mood.

531
00:38:52,950 --> 00:38:55,200
-I suppose I am.  -I won't ask why.

532
00:38:55,660 --> 00:38:58,180
-Small pleasures.  -Your Grace. Lord Tywin.

533
00:38:58,750 --> 00:38:59,660
Prince Oberyn.

534
00:39:00,190 --> 00:39:01,420
I don't believe you have met Ellaria.

535
00:39:01,420 --> 00:39:03,440
This is the Lord Hand Tywin Lannister

536
00:39:03,440 --> 00:39:05,660
and Cersei Lannister the Queen Regent.

537
00:39:05,840 --> 00:39:08,330
I suppose it is former Queen Regent now.

538
00:39:08,770 --> 00:39:11,130
Lord Hand and Lady Cersei,

539
00:39:12,660 --> 00:39:14,030
Ellaria Sand.

540
00:39:14,030 --> 00:39:15,540
My lord. My lady.

541
00:39:16,050 --> 00:39:16,940
Charmed.

542
00:39:18,000 --> 00:39:19,870
Can't say I've ever met a Sand before.

543
00:39:23,820 --> 00:39:25,200
We are everywhere in Dorne.

544
00:39:25,310 --> 00:39:27,530
I have 10,000 brothers and sisters.

545
00:39:27,530 --> 00:39:29,800
Bastards are born of passion, aren't they?

546
00:39:30,180 --> 00:39:31,760
We don't despise them in Dorne.

547
00:39:31,760 --> 00:39:33,070
No? How tolerant of you.

548
00:39:33,070 --> 00:39:35,070
I expect it is a relief, Lady Cersei,

549
00:39:35,300 --> 00:39:37,410
giving up your regal responsibilities.

550
00:39:37,700 --> 00:39:40,100
Wearing the crown for so many years

551
00:39:40,100 --> 00:39:41,070
must have left your neck a bit crooked.

552
00:39:41,070 --> 00:39:42,720
I suppose you'll never know, Prince Oberyn.

553
00:39:42,770 --> 00:39:45,200
It's a shame your older brother couldn't attend the wedding.

554
00:39:45,480 --> 00:39:46,960
Please give him our regards.

555
00:39:47,470 --> 00:39:49,480
With any luck, the gout will abate with time

556
00:39:49,480 --> 00:39:50,800
and he will be able to walk again.

557
00:39:50,800 --> 00:39:52,470
They call it the rich man's disease.

558
00:39:52,870 --> 00:39:54,230
A wonder you don't have it.

559
00:39:54,240 --> 00:39:55,700
Noblemen in my part of the country

560
00:39:55,700 --> 00:39:58,870
don't enjoy the same lifestyle as our counterparts in Dorne.

561
00:39:58,870 --> 00:40:00,660
People everywhere have their differences.

562
00:40:00,960 --> 00:40:03,960
In some places the highborn frown upon those of low birth.

563
00:40:04,090 --> 00:40:07,340
In other places the rape and murder of women and children

564
00:40:07,340 --> 00:40:09,180
is considered distasteful.

565
00:40:11,100 --> 00:40:14,680
What a fortunate thing for you, former Queen Regent,

566
00:40:15,060 --> 00:40:16,430
that your daughter Myrcella has been sent

567
00:40:16,430 --> 00:40:18,220
to live in the latter sort of place.

568
00:40:22,880 --> 00:40:25,830
Everyone, silence! Clear the floor.

569
00:40:28,600 --> 00:40:32,230
There's been too much amusement here today.

570
00:40:32,810 --> 00:40:36,940
A royal wedding is not an amusement.

571
00:40:37,060 --> 00:40:39,290
A royal wedding is history.

572
00:40:39,870 --> 00:40:44,230
The time has come for all of us to contemplate our history.

573
00:40:45,620 --> 00:40:46,680
My lords,

574
00:40:49,330 --> 00:40:50,410
my ladies.

575
00:40:52,290 --> 00:40:53,490
I give you

576
00:40:54,560 --> 00:40:56,400
King Joffrey,

577
00:40:56,990 --> 00:40:59,350
Renly, Stannis,

578
00:40:59,500 --> 00:41:02,610
Robb Stark, Balon Greyjoy.

579
00:41:03,420 --> 00:41:06,180
The War of the Five Kings.

580
00:41:09,630 --> 00:41:11,130
I'm the Rightful King.

581
00:41:12,760 --> 00:41:14,890
-King in the North!  -Yes!

582
00:41:20,060 --> 00:41:22,670
Traitor. You're a traitor.

583
00:41:24,230 --> 00:41:25,790
For the Seven Kingdoms!

584
00:41:30,080 --> 00:41:32,380
Let the war begin.

585
00:41:34,440 --> 00:41:36,300
Renly, you're no king.

586
00:41:37,330 --> 00:41:39,550
Away, degenerate. Away. Away.

587
00:41:41,580 --> 00:41:42,670
Ooh, careful.

588
00:41:42,670 --> 00:41:44,980
-Go on.  -I want you to be my prince.

589
00:41:53,230 --> 00:41:54,150
Stannis!

590
00:41:55,370 --> 00:41:57,320
Who's got the gold now, Stark?

591
00:41:57,850 --> 00:42:00,830
I am the rightful king. Challenge me, ruffian.

592
00:42:01,090 --> 00:42:02,690
-Take that.  -I'm drowning. I'm drowning.

593
00:42:02,690 --> 00:42:04,150
I am the King in the North!

594
00:42:08,980 --> 00:42:10,490
Not wildfire!

595
00:42:19,070 --> 00:42:21,560
Pay each of them 20 gold when this is done.

596
00:42:21,830 --> 00:42:22,760
Yes, my lord.

597
00:42:23,540 --> 00:42:25,530
We'll have to find another way to thank the king.

598
00:42:30,010 --> 00:42:31,060
Charge!

599
00:42:37,110 --> 00:42:38,880
Ready, again.

600
00:42:42,950 --> 00:42:44,570
I am the King in the North!

601
00:42:46,850 --> 00:42:48,140
-Charge!  -Charge!

602
00:42:48,460 --> 00:42:49,570
Yes!

603
00:42:50,390 --> 00:42:51,250
Your head!

604
00:43:28,280 --> 00:43:29,440
Fine, gentlemen.

605
00:43:39,670 --> 00:43:41,340
Well fought. Well fought.

606
00:43:41,710 --> 00:43:44,310
Here you are. Champion's purse.

607
00:43:45,740 --> 00:43:49,960
Though you're not the champion yet, are you?

608
00:43:49,960 --> 00:43:53,930
A true champion defeats all the challengers.

609
00:43:54,860 --> 00:43:56,330
Surely there are others out there

610
00:43:56,330 --> 00:43:58,450
who still dare to challenge my reign.

611
00:44:00,330 --> 00:44:01,150
Uncle.

612
00:44:01,760 --> 00:44:04,170
How about you? I'm sure they have a spare costume.

613
00:44:10,860 --> 00:44:13,390
One taste of combat was enough for me, Your Grace.

614
00:44:13,890 --> 00:44:16,110
I would like to keep what remains of my face.

615
00:44:16,850 --> 00:44:18,360
I think you should fight him.

616
00:44:18,720 --> 00:44:20,130
This was but a poor imitation

617
00:44:20,130 --> 00:44:22,280
of your own bravery on the field of battle.

618
00:44:22,490 --> 00:44:24,960
I speak as a firsthand witness.

619
00:44:25,510 --> 00:44:28,560
Climb down from the high table with your new Valyrian sword

620
00:44:28,700 --> 00:44:32,100
and show everyone how a true king wins his throne.

621
00:44:33,160 --> 00:44:34,310
Be careful, though.

622
00:44:34,770 --> 00:44:37,950
This one is clearly mad with lust.

623
00:44:38,120 --> 00:44:41,320
It would be a tragedy for the king to lose his virtue

624
00:44:41,520 --> 00:44:43,620
hours before his wedding night.

625
00:45:14,680 --> 00:45:15,820
A fine vintage.

626
00:45:16,320 --> 00:45:17,920
Shame that it spilled.

627
00:45:18,920 --> 00:45:19,990
It did not spill.

628
00:45:20,090 --> 00:45:21,750
My love, come back to me.

629
00:45:22,080 --> 00:45:23,790
It's time for my father's toast.

630
00:45:25,890 --> 00:45:27,730
Well, how does he expect me to toast without wine?

631
00:45:31,110 --> 00:45:34,690
Uncle, you can be my cupbearer,

632
00:45:35,610 --> 00:45:37,570
seeing as you're too cowardly to fight.

633
00:45:38,200 --> 00:45:39,840
Your Grace does me a great honor.

634
00:45:40,370 --> 00:45:42,840
It's not meant as an honor.

635
00:46:14,710 --> 00:46:15,790
Bring me my goblet.

636
00:46:38,950 --> 00:46:40,530
What good is an empty cup?

637
00:46:42,200 --> 00:46:43,030
Fill it.

638
00:46:57,770 --> 00:46:58,580
Kneel.

639
00:47:01,560 --> 00:47:02,950
Kneel before your king.

640
00:47:08,410 --> 00:47:09,170
Kneel.

641
00:47:17,290 --> 00:47:18,400
I said,

642
00:47:19,530 --> 00:47:20,670
kneel!

643
00:47:24,310 --> 00:47:25,690
Look, the pie.

644
00:47:40,500 --> 00:47:41,360
My queen.

645
00:47:53,960 --> 00:47:54,970
Wonderful.

646
00:47:57,100 --> 00:47:58,010
Wonderful.

647
00:47:59,680 --> 00:48:00,720
My hero.

648
00:48:05,070 --> 00:48:07,960
-Can we leave now?  -Let's find out.

649
00:48:16,890 --> 00:48:17,730
Uncle.

650
00:48:21,550 --> 00:48:22,480
Where are you going?

651
00:48:22,910 --> 00:48:24,370
You're my cupbearer, remember?

652
00:48:25,060 --> 00:48:27,610
I thought I might change out of these wet clothes, Your Grace.

653
00:48:27,620 --> 00:48:29,990
No, no, no. No, you're perfect the way you are.

654
00:48:31,880 --> 00:48:32,930
Serve me my wine.

655
00:48:39,390 --> 00:48:41,130
Well, hurry up. This pie is dry.

656
00:48:50,380 --> 00:48:51,250
Mm, good.

657
00:48:52,510 --> 00:48:53,570
Needs washing down.

658
00:48:54,930 --> 00:48:56,590
If it please Your Grace, Lady Sansa is very tired.

659
00:48:56,590 --> 00:48:57,610
No.

660
00:48:59,210 --> 00:49:00,910
No, you'll wait here.

661
00:49:07,870 --> 00:49:08,620
Your Grace?

662
00:49:12,550 --> 00:49:13,340
It's nothing.

663
00:49:19,330 --> 00:49:21,150
-He's choking!  -Help the poor boy.

664
00:49:25,160 --> 00:49:27,530
-Idiots, help your king.  -Move away!

665
00:49:31,140 --> 00:49:32,740
-Joffrey! Joffrey!  -Help him!

666
00:49:33,180 --> 00:49:34,800
-Someone help him!  -Joffrey!

667
00:49:37,410 --> 00:49:38,800
-Come with me now.  -Joffrey! Joffrey!

668
00:49:39,370 --> 00:49:41,750
If you want to live, we have to leave.

669
00:49:42,370 --> 00:49:43,290
Don't touch him!

670
00:49:49,510 --> 00:49:50,290
Joffrey.

671
00:49:51,920 --> 00:49:53,780
Please, Joffrey.

672
00:49:55,010 --> 00:49:56,920
Joffrey, what is it?

673
00:49:58,630 --> 00:49:59,380
Help him!

674
00:50:32,650 --> 00:50:33,630
My son.

675
00:50:40,970 --> 00:50:44,170
He's gone. Our king is gone.

676
00:50:45,490 --> 00:50:46,450
He did this.

677
00:50:49,630 --> 00:50:51,460
He poisoned my son,

678
00:50:52,370 --> 00:50:53,390
your king.

679
00:50:54,600 --> 00:50:56,750
Take him. Take him!

680
00:50:57,810 --> 00:50:58,700
Take him!

681
00:50:59,650 --> 00:51:00,710
Take him!

682
00:51:26,610 --> 00:51:32,980
In a coat of gold or a coat of red

683
00:51:33,020 --> 00:51:38,620
a lion still has claws,

684
00:51:38,650 --> 00:51:45,060
and mine are long and sharp, My Lord,*

685
00:51:45,090 --> 00:51:51,100
as long and sharp as yours.

686
00:51:51,130 --> 00:51:57,270
And so he spoke, and so he spoke,

687
00:51:57,310 --> 00:52:03,440
that lord of Castamere,

688
00:52:09,580 --> 00:52:15,990
with no one there to hear.

689
00:52:16,020 --> 00:52:22,100
Yes, now the rains weep o'er his hall,

690
00:52:22,130 --> 00:52:27,970
and not a soul to hear.

